# Create autoagents task from chat

When the **user asks to create a task** in Cursor (not via GitHub Issues), follow this workflow.

## Before creating

1. Run **`./scripts/git-sync-autoagents-branch.sh`** from repo root.
2. Confirm intent: feature (usually needs an issue) vs incident/ops (NEW) vs explicit discard later (**`discarded/`**).

## Choose filename prefix

| Source | Pattern | Example |
|--------|---------|---------|
| User describes work tied to GitHub **#N** | `FEAT-<N>-YYYYMMDD-HHMM-slug.md` | `FEAT-22-20260602-1430-fix-footer-version.md` |
| User describes incident / no issue | `NEW-0-YYYYMMDD-HHMM-slug.md` | `NEW-0-20260602-1430-checkout-500.md` |
| Abandoned before start | `DISCARDED-YYYYMMDD-HHMM-slug.md` in **`autoagents/tasks/discarded/`** | — |

Use **UTC** for `YYYYMMDD-HHMM`. Slug: kebab-case from title (ASCII, max ~40 chars).

## File location and template

- Active tasks: **`autoagents/tasks/`** only (not **`done/`**).
- Copy structure from **`autoagents/tasks/TEMPLATE.md`** or **`autoagents/templates/FEAT_TEMPLATE.md`**.

Minimum sections:

```markdown
# <title>

## Problem / goal
<what and why>

## High-level instructions for coder
- <bullets — no code patches>

## Testing instructions
(filled by coder before UNTESTED-)
```

For FEAT tasks, add **## GitHub Issue** with issue URL and **#N**.

## After creating

- **Do not** implement product code in the same turn unless the user explicitly asks.
- Tell the user the exact path created.
- Optional: if **#N** exists, `gh issue comment` + label **`agent:planned`** per **`docs/agent-loop.md`**.

## Pipeline (for reference)

`FEAT/NEW → WIP → UNTESTED → TESTING → CLOSED → done/YYYY/MM/DD/` via **`scripts/move-agent-task-to-done.sh`**.

See **`autoagents/TASKS-README.md`** for full rules.
